From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: lock the PPE provider while acquiring it

Ethernet drvdata is published before probe has initialized every PPE
resource. Merely finding eth does not prove eth->ppe is ready, nor does
a platform device reference protect its devm state during driver unbind.

Trylock the supplier, require the bound Ethernet driver and initialized
PPE, and add the managed consumer dependency before releasing the lock.
Keep the existing unavailable response and module/device reference
balance, without blocking against supplier-initiated consumer unbind.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -1554,19 +1554,29 @@
 		goto error_pdev_put;
 	}
 
-	eth = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
-	if (!eth)
+	if (!device_trylock(&pdev->dev))
 		goto error_module_put;
+	if (READ_ONCE(pdev->dev.links.status) != DL_DEV_DRIVER_BOUND ||
+	    strcmp(dev_driver_string(&pdev->dev), KBUILD_MODNAME))
+		goto error_unlock;
+
+	eth = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
+	if (!eth || !eth->ppe)
+		goto error_unlock;
 
 	if (!device_link_add(dev, &pdev->dev, DL_FLAG_AUTOREMOVE_CONSUMER)) {
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev,
 			"failed to create device link to consumer %s\n",
 			dev_name(dev));
-		goto error_module_put;
+		goto error_unlock;
 	}
 
+	device_unlock(&pdev->dev);
+
 	return &eth->ppe->dev;
 
+error_unlock:
+	device_unlock(&pdev->dev);
 error_module_put:
 	module_put(THIS_MODULE);
 error_pdev_put:
